WEBVTT

00:00.320 --> 00:02.140
Kazuo, now!

00:02.140 --> 00:02.770
Right!

00:06.730 --> 00:08.230
I'm going for it, Masao!

00:09.150 --> 00:10.820
Okay!

00:10.820 --> 00:12.820
<i>This is...!</i>

00:13.740 --> 00:21.580
Go! This is our new aerial technique... Skylab Hurricane!

00:21.580 --> 00:33.020
<i>Oh my! The Tachibana Twins docked their feet together and one launches the other into the air!</i>

00:36.550 --> 00:39.510
Go!

00:39.510 --> 00:40.840
Morisaki!

00:40.840 --> 00:41.520
Yeah!

00:41.520 --> 00:43.830
<i>It's in!</i>

00:43.830 --> 00:48.280
<i>Here comes a mind-blowing new aerial technique from the Tachibana Twins!</i>

00:48.280 --> 00:50.020
This is...!

00:52.290 --> 00:55.000
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

00:52.290 --> 00:55.000
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

00:55.910 --> 00:58.580
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

00:55.910 --> 00:58.580
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

00:59.500 --> 01:02.210
<i>Ai! Ai! Ai!</i>

00:59.500 --> 01:02.210
<i>Love! Love! Love!</i>

01:09.090 --> 01:11.930
<i>moeru you ni hitori demo</i>

01:09.090 --> 01:11.930
<i>I keep running, lying to myself</i>

01:11.930 --> 01:18.190
<i>ikiteyukeru to usobuite hashiritsudzukete</i>

01:11.930 --> 01:18.190
<i>that I can live alone, though the loneliness makes me burn</i>

01:18.190 --> 01:24.070
<i>unubore no morosa wo kimi wa shitteta na no ni</i>

01:18.190 --> 01:24.070
<i>You knew how fragile my self-conceit makes me</i>

01:24.070 --> 01:30.660
<i>kokoro made uchinomaresareta kono yoru ni</i>

01:24.070 --> 01:30.660
<i>In this night that even shattered my heart</i>

01:30.660 --> 01:34.660
<i>kimi no koe sagasu</i>

01:30.660 --> 01:34.660
<i>I hate how weak I am</i>

01:34.660 --> 01:39.170
<i>kono yowasa ga nikui yo</i>

01:34.660 --> 01:39.170
<i>yearning for your voice</i>

01:39.170 --> 01:44.710
<i>ima sugu torimodoshi ni ikanakya</i>

01:39.170 --> 01:44.710
<i>"I've got to get you back right now!"</i>

01:44.710 --> 01:46.300
<i>baka darou?</i>

01:44.710 --> 01:46.300
<i>I'm stupid, right?</i>

01:46.300 --> 01:47.510
<i>ai</i>

01:46.300 --> 01:47.510
<i>Love!</i>

01:47.510 --> 01:51.010
<i>kizudarake no ai wo shinjite</i>

01:47.510 --> 01:51.010
<i>Believing in my scarred love</i>

01:51.010 --> 02:00.900
<i>nagareochita namida sae mo tsuyosa e to kaete</i>

01:51.010 --> 02:00.900
<i>I will turn these shedded tears into strength</i>

02:00.900 --> 02:01.730
<i>ai</i>

02:00.900 --> 02:01.730
<i>Love!</i>

02:01.730 --> 02:05.530
<i>kizudarake no ai da to shite mo</i>

02:01.730 --> 02:05.530
<i>Even though it is a scarred love</i>

02:05.530 --> 02:09.530
<i>bokura no sekai wo tomoshiteru</i>

02:05.530 --> 02:09.530
<i>it lightens up our world</i>

02:09.530 --> 02:15.790
<i>kono ai mo ichido taritomo</i>

02:09.530 --> 02:15.790
<i>I will not let go of this love</i>

02:15.790 --> 02:18.580
<i>hanasanai</i>

02:15.790 --> 02:18.580
<i>for a single moment!</i>

02:20.410 --> 02:25.910
<b><b>EPISODE 38:
TAKE THEM DOWN! TACHIBANA TWINS</b></b>

02:21.370 --> 02:22.870
<i>2-1!</i>

02:22.870 --> 02:27.120
<i>Hanawa MS have gotten a goal back from their opponent with an incredible aerial technique.</i>

02:28.270 --> 02:31.460
Did you see that? That's our Skylab Hurricane!

02:31.460 --> 02:35.130
We can do it because we're twins. It's the best shot there is!

02:35.130 --> 02:38.930
Damn, they're right. Tachibana Twins' aerial football has evolved.

02:38.930 --> 02:41.270
It's not just an evolution; call it a revolution!

02:41.270 --> 02:47.140
Both Masao and Kazuo have been doing special training day after day, just to get that shot right.

02:52.860 --> 02:54.880
<i>We did it, right Masao?</i>

02:54.880 --> 02:56.850
<i>It's not enough to do it once.</i>

02:56.850 --> 02:58.370
<i>Let's go at it once again!</i>

02:58.370 --> 03:00.320
<i>Are serious? But our legs are—</i>

03:01.740 --> 03:05.200
<i>This time I'll be the bottom. You jump.</i>

03:05.200 --> 03:06.830
<i>Okay, got it...</i>

03:06.830 --> 03:08.830
<i>That's enough, you two.</i>

03:08.830 --> 03:10.500
<i>You can do it again tomorrow.</i>

03:10.500 --> 03:15.940
<i>No! If we can't succeed with it every time we try, then we can't say we've done it.</i>

03:15.940 --> 03:19.170
<i>He's right! If we can't do this, we can't win!</i>

03:19.600 --> 03:20.440
<i>Come on!</i>

03:20.440 --> 03:21.170
<i>Yeah.</i>

03:21.950 --> 03:24.850
We know how much they've worked.

03:29.960 --> 03:35.120
The one thing we can do is to provide full backup for their Skylab Hurricane with all of our might.

03:35.120 --> 03:36.320
Yeah!

03:39.990 --> 03:42.350
That move just now was awesome!

03:42.350 --> 03:45.450
It's like they have no more blind spots, y'know.

03:45.450 --> 03:48.510
So that's the Tachibana Twins' new aerial technique...

03:48.510 --> 03:51.060
You can't exactly call that a surprise attack.

03:51.060 --> 03:54.100
Right. With that, there's no way they'd lose aerial bouts.

03:54.100 --> 03:54.750
Yeah.

03:54.750 --> 03:57.130
<i>What will you do, Tsubasa?</i>

04:03.290 --> 04:05.390
<i>Hyuga...</i>

04:05.390 --> 04:08.180
Skylab Hurricane, huh...

04:09.270 --> 04:11.020
Hey, did you get that?

04:11.020 --> 04:15.360
Yes, I've never seen such an amazing shot before!

04:15.360 --> 04:20.860
With their previous aerial technique, they were turning around and jumping off of the goal.

04:20.860 --> 04:23.530
Shooting from that position was hard.

04:23.530 --> 04:27.820
So they were passing the ball immediately and making it the Triangle Shot.

04:28.410 --> 04:34.880
But with this new aerial technique, the Skylab Hurricane, they can use the power of the jump to shoot directly.

04:34.880 --> 04:39.840
You can't counter that by simply making the goalpost unstable.

04:40.000 --> 04:42.220
This match has become quite the spectacle.

04:42.220 --> 04:44.260
How will Nankatsu react?

04:44.890 --> 04:48.260
How will Tsubasa make a comeback?

04:48.810 --> 04:50.690
Let's all calm down for now.

04:50.690 --> 04:55.420
Come on, we've just been shown an insane special shot.

04:55.420 --> 05:00.850
That sure is an amazing move, but they can't use that move unless they get the ball in front of our goal.

05:00.850 --> 05:01.780
Oh!

05:01.780 --> 05:03.150
That's it!

05:03.150 --> 05:08.780
That means that we'll just have to quickly keep the guy who got the ball in check, and not let him get the ball there.

05:08.780 --> 05:10.340
That, and to attack!

05:10.340 --> 05:12.410
Let's continue this match in Hanawa's side.

05:12.410 --> 05:15.250
Offense is the best kind of defense!

05:15.250 --> 05:16.690
Yes.

05:16.690 --> 05:18.880
All right! Let's focus and keep going!

05:18.880 --> 05:20.550
Yeah!

05:22.530 --> 05:24.550
<i>Don't you lose, Tsubasa.</i>

05:24.550 --> 05:27.720
<i>I will be the one to defeat you!</i>

05:30.720 --> 05:34.600
<i>Myoko MS carries the ball skillfully and shoots!</i>

05:35.530 --> 05:38.850
<i>Wakashimazu firmly catches it again!</i>

05:38.850 --> 05:39.950
That can't be!

05:39.950 --> 05:41.520
Nice, Wakashimazu!

05:42.320 --> 05:46.700
<i>While Hyuga is not here, the main pillar of Toho is Wakashimazu!</i>

05:46.700 --> 05:49.450
<i>We're good enough even if Hyuga isn't here.</i>

05:50.000 --> 05:51.660
<i>He's in top form this tournament.</i>

05:51.660 --> 05:56.080
<i>Thanks to his perfect defense, Wakashimazu has yet to give his opponents a chance to score.</i>

05:56.080 --> 05:59.830
<i>Just like our captain, my only opponent is Nankatsu.</i>

05:59.830 --> 06:02.340
<i>Until I play against Nankatsu, I will not yield a goal!</i>

06:03.380 --> 06:07.220
<i>Hyuga was certain to make his mark during this tournament.</i>

06:07.220 --> 06:13.320
<i>He was certain to be first player to get the title of top scorer 3 years in a row.</i>

06:13.320 --> 06:18.020
<i>Hyuga gave up on all of that, and tied himself down with only Nankatsu.</i>

06:19.050 --> 06:25.300
<i>So we can't afford to lose until the finals!</i>

06:26.580 --> 06:28.610
<i>Hanawa gets the ball!</i>

06:28.610 --> 06:34.080
<i>Right after scoring a goal thanks to the Tachibana Twins' new aerial technique, the mood has completely changed!</i>

06:34.080 --> 06:39.250
<i>The key point in this match is to see whether Hanawa can catch up now or in the second half.</i>

06:40.010 --> 06:41.890
Aimoto, we're going to tie this.

06:41.890 --> 06:42.970
Send it in to the goal!

06:42.970 --> 06:43.750
Okay!

06:43.750 --> 06:45.130
Quick, go check him!

06:45.130 --> 06:46.510
Got it!

06:48.740 --> 06:50.090
<i>As expected of Nankatsu.</i>

06:50.090 --> 06:52.280
<i>They know very well where and how to defend.</i>

06:52.280 --> 06:54.600
<i>They won't let them pass to their goal so easily!</i>

06:57.100 --> 06:58.390
Send me a pass!

07:00.850 --> 07:02.100
I'm cutting that!

07:04.840 --> 07:07.860
<i>Aimoto made it look like he was going to pass and broke away!</i>

07:07.860 --> 07:08.740
Crap!

07:08.740 --> 07:09.690
All right!

07:09.690 --> 07:10.570
Come on!

07:10.570 --> 07:11.820
You bastard!

07:12.580 --> 07:14.870
<i>Ishizaki was a second too late!</i>

07:14.870 --> 07:17.080
<i>The ball is in front of the goal once more.</i>

07:17.080 --> 07:21.540
<i>Now it's time for Masao and Kazuo's, the Tachibana Twins' new aerial technique!</i>

07:21.540 --> 07:24.590
<i>Damn it! They got the ball in front in the end.</i>

07:28.550 --> 07:29.720
<i>What should we do?</i>

07:29.720 --> 07:31.220
Here I go, Masao!

07:32.130 --> 07:35.970
<i>Will they show us Skylab Hurricane again?</i>

07:35.970 --> 07:37.520
<i>What should we do?</i>

07:39.870 --> 07:41.640
<i>Okay, that's it!</i>

07:42.600 --> 07:46.770
<i>Tsubasa jumps using the goalpost!</i>

07:46.770 --> 07:47.520
He flew!

07:47.520 --> 07:49.780
Will he stop the Skylab Hurricane?

07:53.060 --> 07:56.080
<i>What? Unexpectedly, Tachibana Twins don't jump.</i>

07:56.080 --> 07:56.920
What?

07:56.920 --> 07:57.830
Is this a joke?

07:59.450 --> 08:02.160
<i>Tsubasa clears the ball mid-air.</i>

08:03.070 --> 08:05.380
<i>The whistle marks the end of the first half.</i>

08:06.630 --> 08:08.260
That's our Tsubasa!

08:08.260 --> 08:10.590
With this, we can stop the Skylab Hurricane!

08:11.180 --> 08:17.000
<i>You may not know, Tsubasa, but you can't stop our Skylab Hurricane with a jump that's merely that high.</i>

08:17.000 --> 08:19.680
<i>Look forward to the second half.</i>

08:19.680 --> 08:22.690
<i>Tachibana Twins...</i>

08:23.130 --> 08:25.180
Sorry Kazuo, Masao.

08:25.180 --> 08:27.010
That one was a little bit low.

08:27.010 --> 08:27.800
Yes.

08:27.800 --> 08:31.320
Well, that shot really takes a toll on our legs, anyway.

08:31.320 --> 08:33.000
We can't use it recklessly.

08:33.000 --> 08:35.870
We'll use it when we're sure to score.

08:35.870 --> 08:37.870
Tsubasa is amazing!

08:37.870 --> 08:40.950
He counters an aerial technique with another of his own!

08:40.950 --> 08:45.160
However, you can't get too relaxed against the Tachibana Twins' aerial football.

08:45.160 --> 08:47.320
We somehow stopped them this time, but—

08:47.320 --> 08:48.650
It'll be okay!

08:48.650 --> 08:51.610
Tsubasa will make it work!

08:51.610 --> 08:54.120
"Make it work"? Oh, come on...

08:54.120 --> 08:56.000
You're right, Kumi.

08:56.640 --> 09:01.640
If our opponent has gotten better, Tsubasa will get even better.

09:01.640 --> 09:03.390
NANKATSU MIDDLE SCHOOL
SHIZUOKA PREFECTURE

09:03.390 --> 09:06.900
What?! We can't stop them with that jump?

09:06.900 --> 09:11.290
Exactly. They were probably aiming to jump higher.

09:11.290 --> 09:14.260
But since the assist was low, they couldn't.

09:14.260 --> 09:15.970
Damn it! Is that how it is?

09:15.970 --> 09:18.030
This has become quite troublesome.

09:18.030 --> 09:23.540
But since we saw they didn't jump, it's safe to say that move puts a lot of strain on their legs.

09:23.540 --> 09:25.860
So they can't repeat it time after time.

09:25.860 --> 09:27.790
Oh, I see.

09:27.790 --> 09:32.750
So for now, we shouldn't be swept up by our opponent and focus on our own football!

09:32.750 --> 09:33.700
Yeah!

09:33.700 --> 09:35.800
All right!, wait for us, second half!

09:35.800 --> 09:38.300
Let's do this!

09:38.300 --> 09:40.550
HANAWA MIDDLE SCHOOL
AKITA PREFECTURE

09:39.090 --> 09:40.550
Going good, boys!

09:40.550 --> 09:42.930
Keep this up and turn the tables!

09:42.930 --> 09:43.900
Yes!

09:43.900 --> 09:46.560
It's Daimaru's turn in the second half.

09:48.140 --> 09:50.120
We are counting on you, Daimaru!

09:51.360 --> 09:52.400
Okay.

09:52.930 --> 09:53.860
All right!

09:53.860 --> 09:57.860
Now everything is set for us to take Nankatsu down!

09:58.650 --> 10:02.280
<i>There is a player change for Hanawa Middle School.</i>

10:02.280 --> 10:06.790
<i>#3 Takeda is replaced with #12 Daimaru.</i>

10:06.790 --> 10:08.580
Here he is! Daimaru!

10:08.580 --> 10:10.290
We're counting on you!

10:13.550 --> 10:15.730
He's a big one.

10:15.730 --> 10:16.760
Yes.

10:18.220 --> 10:21.890
<i>Now, the second half starts with Hanawa's kick-off.</i>

10:26.770 --> 10:27.960
Cut that ball!

10:27.960 --> 10:29.600
Don't let them attack!

10:29.600 --> 10:30.520
Yeah.

10:31.930 --> 10:32.690
Daimaru!

10:35.410 --> 10:38.900
<i>The ball gets to freshly subbed-in Daimaru.</i>

10:39.780 --> 10:40.990
Here I go!

10:44.000 --> 10:46.370
<i>Daimaru kicks the ball up high!</i>

10:46.370 --> 10:48.580
<i>The ball gets to Nankatsu's goal!</i>

10:48.580 --> 10:49.830
That's preposterous!

10:49.830 --> 10:51.460
That's amazing kicking power!

10:51.460 --> 10:55.800
I was subbed in just because of this kicking power of mine!

10:57.550 --> 10:59.580
This time we'll do it, Kazuo!

10:59.580 --> 11:00.580
Yes!

11:00.580 --> 11:04.290
<i>Nankatsu is in big trouble as soon as the second half starts.</i>

11:05.680 --> 11:07.230
<i>I'll just jump. </i>

11:07.230 --> 11:08.730
<i>I have no choice but to jump and to stop them!</i>

11:10.230 --> 11:11.280
Tsubasa!

11:11.280 --> 11:12.230
It's no use.

11:13.730 --> 11:18.490
<i>Tsubasa, I'll teach you that you can't stop us with that jump .</i>

11:18.490 --> 11:23.780
<i>This time Kazuo acts as the launch pad, and they get into position for Skylab Hurricane.</i>

11:27.540 --> 11:30.660
Go! Our new aerial technique!

11:30.660 --> 11:35.040
Skylab Hurricane!

11:35.040 --> 11:38.050
<i>Here it is! Skylab Hurricane!</i>

11:43.800 --> 11:44.720
Tsubasa...

11:45.970 --> 11:48.970
Tsubasa!

11:49.980 --> 11:51.090
Tsubasa!

11:51.090 --> 11:53.330
That's right! My name means wings, after all!

11:53.330 --> 11:55.190
I can jump high by myself!

11:56.120 --> 11:59.490
<i>Tsubasa jumps using the upper goalpost this time!</i>

12:12.460 --> 12:13.460
Oh...!

12:13.460 --> 12:14.210
What?!

12:17.540 --> 12:20.570
<i>It's a hard clash in mid-air!</i>

12:22.650 --> 12:25.550
<i>The Skylab Hurricane, the Tachibana's great technique, is defeated!</i>

12:25.550 --> 12:26.560
He did it!

12:26.560 --> 12:27.300
Tsubasa!

12:27.300 --> 12:28.310
Masao!

12:28.310 --> 12:30.020
That's Tsubasa for you.

12:30.020 --> 12:30.930
Great!

12:30.930 --> 12:33.810
You are so cool, Tsubasa!

12:34.340 --> 12:37.360
<i>Woah. they've lost their balance!</i>

12:37.360 --> 12:38.140
Masao!

12:38.140 --> 12:38.860
That's not good!

12:40.280 --> 12:41.690
<i>At this rate, his head...!</i>

12:43.940 --> 12:46.570
<i>They fell on their head!</i>

12:46.570 --> 12:47.320
Tsubasa!

12:47.320 --> 12:48.490
Tsubasa...!

12:49.990 --> 12:51.450
Tsubasa!

12:51.450 --> 12:52.430
Masao!

12:52.430 --> 12:54.530
<i>A big accident happened.</i>

12:54.530 --> 12:56.380
<i>The match's paused for now.</i>

12:56.380 --> 12:58.430
<i>Are they injured?</i>

12:58.430 --> 12:59.690
Hey, Tsubasa!

13:00.460 --> 13:02.380
My shoulder is...

13:02.380 --> 13:07.140
<i>It seems Tsubasa who fell first took the most damage.</i>

13:07.140 --> 13:09.400
Are you okay, Masao?

13:09.400 --> 13:12.170
That Tsubasa covered me, and...

13:12.640 --> 13:15.130
Tsubasa!

13:16.380 --> 13:18.400
Boy, are you okay?

13:18.400 --> 13:20.650
Yes.

13:21.290 --> 13:22.820
I'm... fine.

13:22.820 --> 13:24.650
I'm... fine.

13:25.650 --> 13:26.570
That's bad.

13:26.570 --> 13:28.320
You may have dislocated your shoulder.

13:29.040 --> 13:31.560
You must go to the infirmary right away.

13:31.560 --> 13:33.800
Such a little thing wouldn't hinder...

13:33.800 --> 13:35.540
Tsubasa!

13:37.250 --> 13:39.000
I'm fine...

13:39.000 --> 13:41.380
Sir, I am playing.

13:41.380 --> 13:43.880
I definitely am!

13:43.880 --> 13:44.970
Boy...

13:44.970 --> 13:47.170
Tsubasa, it's impossible.

13:47.170 --> 13:48.890
Your face is becoming pale too.

13:48.890 --> 13:50.590
Get treated and come back afterwards.

13:50.590 --> 13:53.210
Yeah, we'll hold them off until then.

13:53.210 --> 13:54.780
I can't do that.

13:54.780 --> 13:56.520
They are right.

13:56.520 --> 13:58.580
Go to the infirmary right away.

13:58.580 --> 14:00.290
This is a referee order.

14:01.190 --> 14:04.190
If you refuse, I will have you ejected from the game for good.

14:06.010 --> 14:07.260
Yes, sir.

14:07.260 --> 14:08.450
Understood...

14:08.450 --> 14:10.120
Sorry, guys.

14:10.120 --> 14:11.610
I'll be back before you know it.

14:11.610 --> 14:15.080
I'm leaving it to you until then, guys.

14:15.080 --> 14:16.960
Count on it!

14:19.900 --> 14:23.590
<i>It seems Tsubasa will be leaving due to an injury.</i>

14:23.590 --> 14:24.820
What?!

14:24.820 --> 14:30.830
<i>Nankatsu have averted the danger of a tied game, but they may have paid too high a price.</i>

14:30.830 --> 14:33.250
<i>Football is a cruel sport.</i>

14:33.250 --> 14:36.990
<i>During the time spent on his treatment, the game cannot be stopped.</i>

14:36.990 --> 14:38.700
Tsubasa...

14:38.700 --> 14:39.810
Sanae!

14:39.810 --> 14:42.020
Nankatsu is in danger.

14:42.420 --> 14:43.770
Tsubasa...

14:43.770 --> 14:45.690
What a disaster...

14:45.690 --> 14:48.510
Nankatsu is driven into a corner.

14:48.510 --> 14:54.370
Depending on the severity of his injury, he might not be able to play for the rest of the tournament.

14:56.700 --> 15:01.000
<i>The ball that crossed the line has been ruled a corner kick for Hanawa.</i>

15:01.000 --> 15:03.660
They will definitely go for that technique.

15:03.660 --> 15:04.990
That's for sure.

15:04.990 --> 15:06.640
Taki and I will block that.

15:06.640 --> 15:08.260
Yeah, we'll show them!

15:08.260 --> 15:09.200
All right, guys!

15:09.200 --> 15:13.090
Listen, until Tsubasa comes back, we won't allow them to tie, no matter what!

15:13.090 --> 15:13.680
Sure!

15:13.680 --> 15:17.960
Tsubasa may have gotten injured to save you, but listen...

15:17.960 --> 15:19.890
We will not hold back.

15:19.890 --> 15:22.010
That's supposed to be the rule of a battle.

15:22.010 --> 15:23.690
I know that, Kazuo.

15:24.160 --> 15:28.360
Let's do it once more! Our Skylab Hurricane!

15:32.910 --> 15:35.330
INFIRMARY

15:35.330 --> 15:36.560
What?

15:36.560 --> 15:37.930
What's happening in there?!

15:39.070 --> 15:41.870
<i>Oh! This is...!</i>

15:43.290 --> 15:44.220
What?!

15:44.220 --> 15:45.710
Is this even allowed?

15:47.090 --> 15:50.410
<i>Nankatsu set up a brave strategy!</i>

15:50.410 --> 15:53.470
<i>Kisugi and Taki are the ones sitting on the goal.</i>

15:53.470 --> 15:56.930
<i>This is a plan just for stopping Skylab Hurricane!</i>

15:56.930 --> 15:59.160
It's the idea Tsubasa gave us.

15:59.160 --> 16:01.450
We can't mimic what he did,

16:01.450 --> 16:04.030
but we can climb on the bar beforehand!

16:04.030 --> 16:07.070
We will defeat Skylab Hurricane with this!

16:08.080 --> 16:09.060
Interesting!

16:09.060 --> 16:10.880
Jump if you will!

16:11.530 --> 16:13.280
Go, Daimaru!

16:13.280 --> 16:13.950
Sure!

16:13.950 --> 16:17.120
<i>Now Masao is the one at the bottom!</i>

16:17.120 --> 16:19.300
All right! Kisugi, Taki!

16:19.300 --> 16:21.640
Jump with all your might and stop that technique!

16:21.640 --> 16:22.580
Sure!

16:22.580 --> 16:23.710
Here I come!

16:24.140 --> 16:26.460
<i>This time it's a low-ball!</i>

16:26.460 --> 16:27.590
What?!

16:27.590 --> 16:28.840
Here I go!

16:30.630 --> 16:33.880
Our Skylab Hurricane isn't just about jumping high!

16:33.880 --> 16:36.640
We can launch at any angle!

16:39.310 --> 16:45.020
Go, Low-Flying Skylab Hurricane!

16:45.430 --> 16:48.520
<i>Kazuo jumps low following the ball.</i>

16:48.520 --> 16:49.760
From below?!

16:49.760 --> 16:50.650
We'll stop it!

16:55.110 --> 16:58.020
<i>It's in! Hanawa scores their second goal!</i>

16:58.020 --> 17:01.540
<i>They've finally tied the game in the 7th minute of the second half!</i>

17:02.430 --> 17:04.050
That's it! It's tied!

17:04.050 --> 17:05.670
We finally caught up!

17:05.670 --> 17:08.170
Nice shot, Masao, Kazuo!

17:08.170 --> 17:10.290
The Skylab Hurricane is invincible!

17:10.290 --> 17:12.140
<i>Great, we can win this.</i>

17:12.140 --> 17:15.260
<i>If we can keep this momentum, we can beat Nankatsu!</i>

17:15.260 --> 17:17.620
All right! Let's take the game over quickly!

17:17.620 --> 17:19.260
It's no good.

17:19.260 --> 17:21.560
If they can launch themselves at any angle,

17:21.560 --> 17:23.480
we have no means to stop that!

17:23.480 --> 17:25.730
INFIRMARY

17:27.520 --> 17:30.040
I guess you've heard the screams.

17:30.040 --> 17:33.200
It was just a little bit of a rough treatment. No need to worry.

17:35.560 --> 17:39.370
Doctor, will he be able to play for the rest of the game?

17:39.370 --> 17:40.060
Huh?

17:40.060 --> 17:41.290
Yup.

17:41.290 --> 17:45.200
This treatment is for to be able to return to the game.

17:45.200 --> 17:49.920
Nankatsu is a team formed around Tsubasa Ozora, after all.

17:49.920 --> 17:54.810
Without their pillar, earning their third consecutive championship would be impossible.

17:54.810 --> 17:56.130
Isn't that true, dear captain?

17:56.720 --> 17:57.300
Yes

17:57.300 --> 17:58.390
Oh...

17:59.310 --> 18:05.390
It's set firmly with the taping, but you should avoid contact as much as possible.

18:05.390 --> 18:09.450
Also, you really shouldn't jump to that height ever again.

18:09.450 --> 18:10.150
Yeah.

18:10.150 --> 18:14.420
In the unlikely event that your shoulder dislocates again,

18:14.420 --> 18:17.490
you won't be able to play for the rest of the game.

18:17.490 --> 18:21.140
I simply won't let you back out there.

18:21.140 --> 18:22.240
Keep that in mind. Got it?

18:22.240 --> 18:23.410
Understood.

18:24.720 --> 18:26.260
Thank you very much.

18:28.250 --> 18:29.010
Hm?

18:31.810 --> 18:33.880
Do your best, Tsubasa.

18:34.280 --> 18:35.590
Sure.

18:39.060 --> 18:39.590
Tsubasa.

18:39.940 --> 18:40.850
Are you okay?

18:40.850 --> 18:42.100
What about the game?

18:42.840 --> 18:43.920
It's tied, I see.

18:43.920 --> 18:45.520
They got us.

18:45.520 --> 18:49.020
The Skylab Hurricane can launch at any angle.

18:49.020 --> 18:51.230
What? Did you say any angle?

18:51.230 --> 18:52.080
Take it!

18:52.080 --> 18:52.860
Got you!

18:52.860 --> 18:54.510
<i>They cut the pass in no time!</i>

18:54.510 --> 18:55.230
Stop them!

18:55.230 --> 18:57.320
Let's quickly turn this around!

19:00.950 --> 19:02.160
Tsubasa!

19:02.160 --> 19:06.910
<i>Just now, Tsubasa's returned from his treatment and waits at the side of the pitch.</i>

19:07.380 --> 19:09.850
Guys, focus on the game!

19:09.850 --> 19:12.040
I will fight alongside with you for sure!

19:12.040 --> 19:12.930
Damn.

19:12.930 --> 19:14.800
So he is able to play after all.

19:14.800 --> 19:15.950
Tsubasa!

19:15.950 --> 19:18.320
It wouldn't be fun otherwise.

19:18.320 --> 19:19.170
You said it.

19:19.170 --> 19:22.620
Tsubasa won't be able to get in if there is no dead ball.

19:22.620 --> 19:24.680
We will take the lead before that can happen!

19:24.680 --> 19:27.930
And it will be with this Skylab Hurricane!

19:27.930 --> 19:29.210
It's coming again.

19:29.210 --> 19:31.480
Don't let them cross the ball in front of the goal!

19:31.480 --> 19:32.440
Yeah!

19:32.440 --> 19:35.480
<i>Nankatsu goes to mark Daimaru!</i>

19:35.890 --> 19:36.610
Here.

19:38.320 --> 19:39.150
Go!

19:39.660 --> 19:41.950
<i>Aimoto has lifted the ball this time!</i>

19:41.950 --> 19:42.910
Crap!

19:46.870 --> 19:48.450
Here I go, Masao!

19:49.290 --> 19:52.460
<i>It's a desperate situation for Nankatsu!</i>

19:52.460 --> 19:53.420
Guys!

19:54.800 --> 19:57.170
Go, Skylab...!

19:57.170 --> 19:57.960
We've got them!

19:57.960 --> 19:59.170
It's a turn-around!

20:00.220 --> 20:01.720
Ah!

20:01.720 --> 20:03.720
{Kazuo, you should have lose weight boi}

20:03.090 --> 20:03.980
What?!

20:03.980 --> 20:05.350
<i>They can't jump!</i>

20:05.350 --> 20:06.390
<i>It's broken now!</i>

20:06.390 --> 20:10.000
<i>The Tachibana Twins have failed to perform the Skylab Hurricane!</i>

20:10.000 --> 20:10.810
Masao!

20:10.810 --> 20:11.520
Kazuo!

20:11.520 --> 20:13.130
So it's taken its toll, huh?

20:13.130 --> 20:14.200
Damn it!

20:14.200 --> 20:16.610
<i>It seems like both of their legs are cramping.</i>

20:16.610 --> 20:18.610
We've been saved somehow.

20:18.610 --> 20:19.560
Yeah.

20:19.560 --> 20:24.320
What Tsubasa said before about it taking a big toll on their legs was true after all.

20:25.690 --> 20:27.000
<i>Here he comes!</i>

20:27.000 --> 20:31.660
<i>Nankatsu's Captain Tsubasa has returned after a brief withdrawal from this battle!</i>

20:31.660 --> 20:33.660
Tsubasa, good luck!

20:33.660 --> 20:35.310
Tsubasa, we are counting on you!

20:35.310 --> 20:37.880
We've been waiting for you, Tsubasa!

20:37.880 --> 20:40.670
<i>So you've come back, Tsubasa.</i>

20:40.670 --> 20:41.580
Tsubasa!

20:41.580 --> 20:43.120
Is your shoulder okay?

20:43.120 --> 20:44.430
Yeah, it's okay.

20:44.430 --> 20:46.220
Sorry, Tsubasa.

20:46.220 --> 20:47.820
We messed up and let them tie the game.

20:47.820 --> 20:49.560
It's just a tie.

20:49.560 --> 20:51.090
Don't worry guys, don't worry!

20:51.090 --> 20:52.180
Tsubasa...

20:52.180 --> 20:55.570
If they've caught up with us, all we need to do is to pull away again.

20:55.570 --> 20:59.320
Let's show them the offense we had at the start of the first half once more!

20:59.320 --> 21:00.820
Yeah!

21:00.820 --> 21:04.270
We need to defend until these legs of ours recover, I suppose.

21:04.270 --> 21:08.880
At most, we'll only be able to use the Skylab Hurricane once more this game.

21:08.880 --> 21:11.860
We will fend Nankatsu's offense off until then.

21:11.860 --> 21:12.830
Yeah!

21:12.830 --> 21:16.330
<i>The match resumes with Nankatsu's goal kick!</i>

21:16.330 --> 21:21.590
<i>Now that they have 11 players once again, what kind of recovery will Nankatsu show us?</i>

21:22.570 --> 21:23.260
Tsubasa!

21:23.260 --> 21:24.420
Counting on you!

21:25.500 --> 21:30.430
<i>I can't slip my way in front of the goal where physical play is intense, because I need to avoid contact.</i>

21:30.430 --> 21:33.890
<i>Then I have to stay in the middle and do the playmaking,</i>

21:33.890 --> 21:36.650
<i>make use of everyone and get the score.</i>

21:37.400 --> 21:41.980
<i>The Tachibana Twins mark Taki and Kisugi man-to-man!</i>

21:41.980 --> 21:44.490
<i>These two—who usually focus on offense—are back on defense,</i>

21:44.490 --> 21:47.860
<i>and the others also stay behind the midfield line to tighten the defense.</i>

21:47.860 --> 21:52.700
<i>Do they plan to protect this tied score until the Tachibana Twins' legs have recovered?</i>

21:52.700 --> 21:54.470
<i>Hey, you should focus on the match!</i>

21:54.470 --> 21:55.710
<i>Here is a chance for me!</i>

21:55.710 --> 21:57.170
Tsubasa, he is coming for it!

21:57.170 --> 21:59.230
<i>I can't have my way in front of the goal.</i>

21:59.230 --> 22:01.070
<i>I can't use Kisugi or Taki either.</i>

22:01.070 --> 22:04.170
<i>Then, there is only a single chance to score for me.</i>

22:05.060 --> 22:05.970
What?!

22:13.290 --> 22:17.220
The only thing for it is my Drive Shot!

22:38.750 --> 22:44.800
<i>chotto are mi na ace ga tooru</i>

22:38.750 --> 22:44.800
<i>Hey, look over there at the ace passing through</i>

22:44.800 --> 22:50.800
<i>suguremono zo to machijû sawagu</i>

22:44.800 --> 22:50.800
<i>He's the best, and the whole town cheers him on</i>

22:50.800 --> 22:56.850
<i>chô-chô samba, zigzag samba</i>

22:50.800 --> 22:56.850
<i>Butterfly samba, zig-zag samba</i>

22:56.850 --> 23:01.480
<i>aitsu no uwasa de chamba mo hashiru</i>

22:56.850 --> 23:01.480
<i>Even little old ladies go around talking about him</i>

23:03.110 --> 23:07.780
<i>sore ni tsukete mo ore-tacha nan na no</i>

23:03.110 --> 23:07.780
<i>So, even if we have him, who are we?</i>

23:09.110 --> 23:15.200
<i>ball hitotsu ni kiri-kiri mai sa</i>

23:09.110 --> 23:15.200
<i>The ball spins round and round</i>

23:15.200 --> 23:21.250
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:21.250 --> 23:25.710
<i>itsuka kimeru ze inazuma shoot</i>

23:21.250 --> 23:25.710
<i>One day, I'll score with a lightning shot!</i>

23:27.010 --> 23:33.350
<i>son toki ore ga super hero sa</i>

23:27.010 --> 23:33.350
<i>When that happens, I'll become a super hero!</i>

23:33.350 --> 23:39.390
<i>Dash, dash, dash! Kick and dash!</i>

23:39.390 --> 23:45.690
<i>moete seishun kakenukero</i>

23:39.390 --> 23:45.690
<i>This fierce youth is on the field!</i>

23:49.990 --> 23:59.990
COMING UP, EPISODE 39:
NANKATSU VS. HANAWA - CONCLUSION!
